# The Vercel CLI uploads the whole project directory, not just the
# outputDirectory named in vercel.json. Without this file that means ~800 extra
# files and 186MB per deploy -- output/ (screenshots, Lighthouse runs,
# competitor research), _zh-archive/, docs/, prototypes/ and the loose .xlsx /
# .png artifacts in the repo root.
#
# This site is plain static files, so a deployment needs exactly two things:
# public/ and vercel.json. An allowlist is used rather than a deny list so that
# a new scratch directory added later cannot silently start shipping.
#
# Pattern note: "/*" matches top-level entries only, and re-including /public
# re-includes everything under it (gitignore semantics forbid re-including a
# child whose parent is still excluded, so the parent must be un-ignored).
/*
!/public
!/vercel.json
